<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Johor</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Johor is a state at the southern tip of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malay-peninsula">Malay Peninsula</a>, which became the seat of a Malay sultanate after the fall of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malacca">Malacca</a>. Like Malacca, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/penang">Penang</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/singapore">Singapore</a>, it functioned as a commercial <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/entrepot">entrepôt</a>. The site cites it as part of the trading tradition established by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/srivijaya">Srivijaya Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/johor.jpg" alt="Johor" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mrmw, Mike Rohsopht · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Johor.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
